@page "/om-itmartin"
@inject SiteUseCases Site

@* The "Om mig" tab (user 2026-10-27: "should there be more tabs and fewer boxes?" -> "do it"): who Martin is ("Hvem er ITMartin?"
   tabs from the forside page in Svar), the tiles about his work and other sites, and his posts. The front page keeps only the
   head box, Vidste du and the sign-up. *@
<PageTitle>Om mig · Martin Hvidberg</PageTitle>
@* Calmer since 2026-10-27 (user: "should be prettier and more calm"): a quiet head with the one photo and the contact buttons
   (no separate contact box), soft buttons. Since 2026-10-29 each part is its own box again (user).
   Only the look changed - the words are Martin's own, from Svar -> Sider. *@
<div class="hj-calm">
<PageHead Title="Om mig" Tag="Hvem er ITMartin?" Line="Hvem jeg er, hvad jeg laver – og hvad jeg har lavet." Calm="true">
    <p class="hj-head-note" id="kontakt">Skriv, ring eller send en mail – første snak er altid gratis.</p>
    <div class="hj-head-btns">
        <a class="k-btn" href="/chat-med-martin">Chat med mig</a>
        <a class="k-btn" href="mailto:ITMartin@Mensa.dk">ITMartin@Mensa.dk</a>
        <a class="k-btn" href="tel:+4531194730">31 19 47 30</a>
    </div>
</PageHead>

@* All of Martin's photos live here now - not on the other tabs (user 2026-11-23). *@
<section class="k-card hj-page hj-sec">
    <h2>Billeder af mig</h2>
    <ul class="hj-me-gallery">
        @foreach (var p in MartinPhotos.All)
        {
            <li><img src="@p.Src" alt="Martin Hvidberg@(p.Place.Length > 0 ? " – " + p.Place : "")" width="150" height="150" loading="lazy" />@if (p.Place.Length > 0) { <span>@p.Place</span> }</li>
        }
    </ul>
</section>

<CascadingValue Name="Plain" Value="true">
@* Every part its own box again, like the boxes around them (user 2026-10-29: "all these should also be in the boxes over them");
   was one calm card with rows since 2026-10-27. "Hvem er ITMartin?" open, the rest closed until opened (remembered per phone). *@
@* "Hvem er ITMartin?" tabs HIDDEN 2026-11-23 (user: "only relevant things" - the intro below says the same). *@
@* Martin's own "Om mig og kontakt" text (Svar -> Sider -> om-mig), each "## " part a box. *@
@if (_about is not null)
{
    var (intro, parts) = Sections.Split(_about.Body);
    @if (intro.Length > 0) { <section class="k-card hj-page">@TinyMarkdown.Render(intro)</section> }
    @* "Kontakt mig" box hidden (2026-11-23) - the contact buttons are at the top. *@
    <SectionBoxes Parts="@Relevant(parts)" FirstOpen="false" />
}

@* WorkTiles ("Om mig og mit arbejde", "Mine andre sider") and the Bogshoppen box HIDDEN 2026-11-23 (user: "only relevant things"). *@
</CascadingValue>

@* "Seneste" + "Tidslinje" posts and the family lock HIDDEN 2026-11-23 (user: "only relevant things"). *@
</div>

@code {
    // "Kontakt mig" is the buttons at the top - not a box too (user 2026-11-23: "only relevant things").
    private static List<Sections.Part> Relevant(List<Sections.Part> parts) =>
        parts.Where(x => !x.Title.Trim().Equals("Kontakt mig", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)).ToList();

    [CascadingParameter] private Task<AuthenticationState>? AuthTask { get; set; }

    private Page? _hero;   // Svar -> Sider -> "forside"
    private Page? _about;  // Svar -> Sider -> "om-mig"
    private List<Post> _posts = [];
    private int _hiddenFamily;
    private bool _family, _owner;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var user = AuthTask is null ? null : (await AuthTask).User;
        _family = user.IsFamily();
        _owner = user.IsOwner();
        var front = await Site.FrontAsync(_family);
        (_hero, _posts, _hiddenFamily) = (front.Hero, front.Posts, front.HiddenFamily);
        _about = await Site.PageBySlugAsync("om-mig");
    }
}
